1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
In China, everyone eats off the same shared plates. Warm tradition, or germ nightmare?
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
The dishes don't come to you — they sit in the middle, for the whole table.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,300
A spinning tray, the "lazy Susan," lets you reach every dish without standing up.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,800
Twist: that spinning table was invented in 1915 to fight germs, not for comfort.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:17,200
Dr. Wu Lien-teh added separate serving chopsticks — gōngkuài — to keep shared food clean.

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,400
So — reach for the serving chopsticks, or just dig in with your own? Pick a side.
